# Template for OpenAI's Codex CLI, or any other CLI coding agent this
# switchboard doesn't ship built-in support for. UNVERIFIED: Codex CLI's
# actual first-run prompts (if any) and whether it has its own hosted
# remote-session link haven't been checked against this switchboard — adjust
# CMD and, if needed, add STARTUP_MATCH_N/STARTUP_SEND_N pairs (see
# claude.engine for the pattern) to match whatever your installed version
# actually shows on first run in a new directory. Then rename this file to
# drop the ".example" suffix to enable it — files ending in .example are
# never loaded.
#
# No URL_REGEX is set here, so until/unless you confirm Codex CLI prints its
# own hosted link and add one, the switchboard falls back to its built-in
# ttyd web terminal for this engine automatically — a working default for
# any CLI tool, verified or not.
LABEL=Codex
CMD=codex {name}
